From 94e7b5ae4598d7c238e24090daeab1a7f4ba1c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tamar Christina <tamar.christina@arm.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:41:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AArch64: have -mcpu=native make educated guess on minimum
 arch level

When -mcpu=native encounters a CPU whose MIDR we don't recognize, we currently
fall back to generic-armv8-a and add the extensions reported in /proc/cpuinfo.

For a CPU reporting SVE2, we can make a better guess and use generic-armv9-a as
the starting point.  This patch uses the detected extensions to choose between
the two generic CPUs.  The -march=native path uses the architecture of that CPU,
and unknown heterogeneous systems use the same fallback.

The important detail is that SVE2 doesn't establish all the other features
enabled by the Armv9 baseline.  For example, if cpuinfo reports SVE2 but doesn't
report atomics, we still need to turn off LSE.  The existing extension-string
handling already does this for features with cpuinfo tokens.

There is also a less obvious case: PREDRES is part of the Armv9 baseline but has
no cpuinfo token. For a known CPU we can use the architecture from the CPU table
to establish support.  For an unknown CPU we only have the inferred baseline, so
inheriting PREDRES from it would be an unsupported assumption.

This patch therefore limits the unreported features we inherit for unknown CPUs
to the Armv8-A baseline.  The extension-string handling then adds the reported
extensions and disables unverified defaults from the inferred architecture.

For example, an unknown CPU reporting SVE2 and all the reportable Armv9-A
baseline features gives

  -mcpu=generic-armv9-a+crc+nopredres

Here PREDRES remains disabled because cpuinfo cannot establish it.  With fewer
reported features, the option string also disables the missing baseline
extensions.  Without SVE2 we continue to select generic-armv8-a.

The lookup includes extensions that depend on SVE2, so later SVE2 versions can
also guide the selection even though the parsed feature flags aren't
transitively closed.

The tests cover unknown single-core and heterogeneous systems, both native CPU
and architecture selection, the fallback without SVE2, and the case with all
reportable Armv9-A baseline features present.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/aarch64/driver-aarch64.cc (DEFAULT_ARCH, DEFAULT_CPU):
	Remove.
	(get_cpu_from_ext): New function.  Select a generic CPU using
	SVE2 and extensions that depend on it.
	(host_detect_local_cpu): Use the inferred generic CPU and its
	architecture for unknown CPUs, including heterogeneous systems.
	Limit inherited features without cpuinfo tokens to the Armv8-A
	baseline when the CPU is unknown.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_16.c: Update the expected
	architecture and extensions for the generic Armv9 fallback.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_17.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_34.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/info_37: New cpuinfo fixture for an
	unknown CPU with SVE2.1 and missing Armv9 baseline features.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/info_38: New cpuinfo fixture for an
	unknown CPU without SVE2.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/info_41: New cpuinfo fixture for an
	unknown CPU with SVE2 and all reportable Armv9-A baseline features.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_37.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_38.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_39.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_40.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/aarch64/cpunative/native_cpu_41.c: New test.

(cherry picked from commit 818745a862daee49a02a54202f26972f7cf622cd)
